    "note": "Package-owned oracle seam. evaluate(point) takes a mapping of qualified entry keys to floats and returns a mapping of qualified channel names to floats; it wraps the independent pure-Python oracle verify_stellaris.py, which is imported and never modified. The module also publishes a fixed-name companion, operand_bindings() -> {constraint_id: {source_name: {kind, key}}}, which says which qualified input key or channel each predicate operand means. A generic verifier requires both and fails closed on anything unresolved: on this package one operand of five constraints resolves to nothing by name at all, so a tool that inferred bindings would compare the wrong number and read as a pass.",
